-- NEWER VGM SEGA/Atlus — "Section 17 - Other" sub-batch B (1999-2003 + Billy Hatcher + Ollie King)
--
-- Source: reference/NEWER VGM Sound Sources - SEGAAtlus.csv lines 2979-3341.
-- 15 game/album records, ~336 usage rows.
--
-- This is the dominant sub-batch by row count: Billy Hatcher (~150
-- rows) and Ollie King + its album release (~108 rows) together account
-- for more than three-quarters of the rows here.
--
-- Composer credits this batch:
--   - JRA PAT for Dreamcast       — Hideki Naganuma
--   - J. League Pro Soccer Club o Tsukurou! 3 — Hideki Naganuma
--   - Riviera: The Promised Land  — Minako Adachi, Shigeki Hayashi, Toshiaki Sakoda
--                                   (applied to both the GBA and PSP entries)
--   - Ollie King                  — Hideki Naganuma
--
-- New manufacturers introduced this batch:
--   - Ubiquity (Brooklyn Beats sample library, Billy Hatcher)
--
-- New products this batch (selection — all INSERT OR IGNORE):
--   - Clavia / Nord Lead 2, Nord Rack 2
--   - e-LAB / XTc Files of Techno
--   - EDIROL / STUDIO Canvas SD-90
--   - E-MU Systems / ESI-32 150MB Production SoundSet, Orbit 9090
--   - KORG / Trinity proX, TRITON
--   - Roland / SR-JV80-17 Country Collection
--   - Best Service / Barbara Dennerlein B3
--   - EastWest / Jeff Skunk Baxter Skunkworks, Chronic Horns
--   - Sonic Foundry / Bill Laswell's Sample Material
--   - Sound Ideas / The General Series 6000
--   - AMG / Diffusion Series: The Next Generation
--   - AMG & Hit Music / Norman Cook - Skip to my Loops
--   - Sounds Good & Steinberg / Hip-Hop Beats & Treats  (with hyphen;
--     existing "Hip Hop Beats & Treats" no-hyphen entry from S3 kept
--     distinct per Rule 2)
--   - Big Fish Audio / Big Beat - Megaton Bomb Vol. 4
--   - PrimeSounds / Methods of Mayhem II - Damage Control
--     (existing "Methods of Mayhem II" entry from S13 kept distinct per Rule 2)
--   - Masterbits / Climax-Collection Vol. 3 - Guitars
--   - MOTU / Digital Performer 3, Digital Performer 4 Extras Disc
--   - PowerFX / Lo-Fi and Illbient Sound FX, The Love & Pop String Thing!
--   - Ubiquity / Brooklyn Beats
--   - UltimateSoundBank / Soundscan Vol. 16 - Bossa Brazil,
--     Soundscan Vol. 18 - Funky Vocals,
--     Soundscan Vol. 26 - Big Beat Vol. 2 Samples,
--     Soundscan Vol. 46 - 70's Breakbeats
--   - Vengeance Sound / Essential House Vol. 2
--   - Zero-G / Cuckooland Vol. 1 Unhinged, Ethnic, Ethnic 2,
--             The Operating Table, Rhythm Guitar & FX
--
-- Game-record split for Riviera (CSV rows 3059-3071):
--   The CSV lists Riviera: The Promised Land's WonderSwan original
--   (2002-07-12, no usage rows), then a "Game Boy Advance" sub-header
--   (2004-11-25, 7 main + 1 stuff), then a "Playstation Portable"
--   sub-header (2006-11-22, 1 main). We split into two distinct game
--   records — Riviera GBA and Riviera PSP — since they have different
--   release dates and platform-specific usage rows. The WS original
--   has no rows attached so it isn't created.
--
-- Game-record split for Ollie King (CSV rows 3224-3341):
--   Ollie King has two sections in the CSV: the game proper (March 2004),
--   then "Ollie King Soundtrack (Album Release)" (no date in CSV). These
--   are treated as two separate game records ("Ollie King" and "Ollie
--   King Soundtrack (Album Release)") following the Section 1 Atlus
--   arrange-album convention.
--
-- Verbatim preservations (Rule 2):
--   - "Ueberschall " (trailing space on Skunkworks J. League row T3056)
--     is normalised to "Ueberschall" — trailing whitespace is not a
--     distinct manufacturer.
--   - Composite uncertainty markers in product field preserved as
--     raw_source: e.g. "KORG - ? (01R/W or 01R/W Card)" (Vampire Night
--     T3028), "Roland - ? (SOUND Canvas SC-88 Pro or JV-2080)" — though
--     the SC-88 Pro / JV-2080 form appears in Other-c, not this batch.
--   - "Hip-Hop Beats & Treats" (with hyphen, Ollie King album release)
--     kept distinct from existing "Hip Hop Beats & Treats" (no hyphen,
--     Daytona USA). Punctuation difference is NOT a case difference;
--     NOCASE does not merge them.
--   - "Methods of Mayhem II - Damage Control" (Let's Tap, Other-c) kept
--     distinct from existing "Methods of Mayhem II" (Yakuza, S13) — but
--     this row is in Other-c, not this batch. Listed in the new-products
--     summary above for tracker continuity only.
--
-- Position numbering: per-game positions start at 1 and run monotonically
-- across main and stuff_to_find.

